        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T12:24:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI: change 550182 removes the leakage of JGit’s transitive dependency\nclosure (jgit_deps) into release.war.\n\nThis intentionally demonstrates the risk introduced by splitting JGit’s\ncompile-time dependency graph from Gerrit’s runtime classpath: tests still\nexecute with JGit’s full transitive closure available, while the WAR is\nbuilt without it, even though avoiding version skew is desirable and\nintentional.\n\nAs a result, CI may pass while the produced release.war fails at runtime\nwith missing dependencies (e.g. commons-io via commons-compress 1.28),\nexposing false-positive integration test results.\n\nExcept for explicitly documented and accepted limitations, false-positive\nintegration test results for a release artifact should not occur and\nsignificantly reduce confidence in the current dependency model.",
      "parentUuid": "4ba810d2_a39342a0",
